    "country": "Japan"
  },
  "presentation_summary": [
    "81-year-old man with CKD, diabetes, prostate cancer, and chronic dexamethasone plus prednisolone exposure presented with progressive right thigh pain, erythema, swelling, and worsening pain after antibiotics.",
    "Admission vitals showed clear consciousness, HR 100, RR 24, BP 130/93, temperature 37.1 C, and O2 saturation 98% on room air.",
    "Labs showed leukocytosis/neutrophilia, severe lymphopenia, anemia, thrombocytopenia, creatinine 4.09 mg/dL, and CRP 22.1 mg/dL.",
    "Debridement found yeasts in fascia; on day 3 he developed septic shock, coma, new right-arm skin lesion, and cryptococcal meningitis.",
    "Cryptococcus neoformans was cultured from blood, right thigh fascia, CSF, and later right-arm tissue.",
    "Despite liposomal amphotericin B, flucytosine, debridements, ventilation, and transfusion, he developed DIC-like bleeding, hepatic failure, profound thrombocytopenia, and died on day 11."
  ],
